{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trees"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Trees"}],"title":"Trees","externalID":"Trees"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/AllBinaryTrees","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/BinaryTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/NotATree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/OrderedTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/PrefixTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"],"title":"Structures","generated":true},{"anchor":"Functions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/prefixTree(of:)"],"title":"Functions","generated":true},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/GraphProtocols"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/RootedTree":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"RootedTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RootedTree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RootedTree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree with a root: an undirected "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent(of:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"depth(of:)"},{"text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preorder"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Forest":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Forest","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest","abstract":[{"text":"A forest: an acyclic undirected graph, possibly empty, so a disjoint union of trees (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trees"},{"text":" lists them by least vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"text":" says which one a vertex is in.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/OrderedTree":{"kind":"symbol","title":"OrderedTree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/OrderedTree","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrderedTree"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrderedTree"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/orderedtree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered tree (plane tree): a rooted tree in which the children of each vertex form a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence, first to last. The order is part of the value: two ordered trees are equal when they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have the same root and every vertex has the same children in the same order, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity being an ordered-tree isomorphism between them."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/prefixTree(of:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/prefixtree(of:)","abstract":[{"text":"The prefix tree of ","type":"text"},{"code":"sequences","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": one vertex per distinct prefix (the root, 0, is the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one), one edge per vertex but the root, labelled with the symbol it appends, and the vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where each sequence ends. Repeated sequences end at the same vertex, and an empty sequence at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the root.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"prefixTree(of:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"prefixTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrefixTree","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees10PrefixTreeV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/prefixTree(of:)"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/BinaryTree":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A binary tree: a rooted tree in which each vertex has at most a left child and a right child,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by position. A vertex with only a left child is a different tree from one with only a right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"child. Two binary trees are equal when they have the same root and every vertex has the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left and right children."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/binarytree","title":"BinaryTree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/BinaryTree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BinaryTree","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/PrefixTree":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/PrefixTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrefixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/prefixtree","role":"symbol","title":"PrefixTree","abstract":[{"text":"The prefix tree (trie) of some sequences: an arborescence on ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rooted at 0, the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prefix, in which each vertex is a distinct prefix of a sequence and each edge appends one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol. ","type":"text"},{"code":"prefixTree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builds it.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PrefixTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/AllBinaryTrees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/AllBinaryTrees","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"AllBinaryTrees","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AllBinaryTrees"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AllBinaryTrees"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/allbinarytrees","abstract":[{"text":"Every binary tree on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"text":" in Knuth’s Algorithm B order, its vertices numbered in preorder:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree.allBinaryTrees(vertexCount:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent. As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the parent (zero or one), and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","title":"Arborescence"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/NotATree":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NotATree","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NotATree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/notatree","abstract":[{"text":"The error a checked conversion throws when its input is not one tree, such as a shortest-path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forest grown from several sources given to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(checked:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"NotATree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/NotATree"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees":{"url":"\/documentation\/trees","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"Trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Tree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}],"type":"topic"}}}